o unravel the Enigma machine. It tells of how, under the very noses of the Germans, Enigma code-breaking continued in Vichy France. And how code-breakers from Poland continued their work for Her Majesty's Secret Service, watching the USSR's first steps of the Cold War. The people of X, Y and Z were eccentric, colourful and caught up in world events that they could watch not control. This is their story ...\"--Publisher description"},"tableOfContents":{"@type":"Contents","#text":"List of maps -- Foreword -- Dramatic personae -- Timeline -- Introduction -- Nulle part -- Enter the king -- Mighty pens -- The Scarlet Pimpernels -- How they brought the good news from Ghent to Aix -- Monstrous pile -- The mirror crack'd from side to side -- Into three parts -- A mystery inside an enigma -- Hide and seek -- The last play -- Epilogue -- Appendix -- Notes -- Abbreviations -- Select bibliography -- Index."},"note":[{"@type":"statement of responsibility","#text":"Dermot Turing."},{"@type":"bibliography","#text":"Includes bibliographical references and index."}],"subject":[{"geographicCode":{"@authority":"marcgac","#text":"e-uk---"}},{"@authority":"lcsh","name":{"@type":"corporate","namePart":"Government Code and Cypher School (Great Britain)"}},{"@authority":"fast","name":{"@type":"corporate","namePart":"Government Code and Cypher School (Great Britain)"}},{"@authority":"fast","temporal":"1939-1945"},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"Enigma cipher system"},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":["World War, 1939-1945","Military intelligence"],"geographic":"Great Britain"},{"@authority":"rvm","topic":"Enigma (Machine à chiffrer)"},{"@authority":"eflch","topic":"Warfare and Defence"},{"@authority":"fast","topic":"Enigma cipher system"},{"@authority":"fast","topic":"Military intelligence"},{"@authority":"ukslc","topic":"Warfare and Defence"},{"@authority":"fast","geographic":"Great Britain"}],"classification":[{"@authority":"lcc","#text":"D810.C88 T87 2018"},{"@edition":"23","@authority":"ddc"